---
export interface Props {
  title?: string;
  titleleft?: string;
  titleright?: string;
  as?: "h1" | "h2" | "h3" | "h4" | "h5" | "h6";
}
const { title, titleleft, titleright, as: HeadingTag = "h2" } = Astro.props;

// The title badge is `absolute -top-6`, so the width cap (w-[92%] max-w-2xl)
// plus text-center and the card's pt-32/md:pt-28 are load bearing — a full docx
// sentence has to wrap rather than blow past the viewport, and the wrapped badge
// has to clear the grid below it. There is no whitespace-nowrap here and none
// may come back.
//
// Re-measured against RENGER8888's H2-5 title, the sentence this brand feeds it
// ("โปรโมชั่นสุดคุ้มควรเทียบมากกว่าแค่จำนวนโบนัส", 43 chars). Mobile at a 375px
// viewport: the card is 343px inside the section's px-4, the badge is w-[92%] =
// 316px, and after px-4 (32px) and border-2 (4px) about 280px is left (this
// variant has no ✦ spans eating width). text-lg wraps that title to 2 lines, 3
// at worst; leading-normal on 18px = 27px a line, so 3×27 + 20 (py-2.5) + 4
// (border-2) = 105px tall, bottom edge at 105 − 24 = 81px into the card — clear
// of pt-32 (128px). Desktop: md:text-2xl at 36px a line over ~604px of usable
// width inside max-w-2xl wraps to 2 lines at worst = 96px tall, bottom edge at
// 72px, inside md:pt-28 (112px). Both clear as they stand; do not shrink either.
// pt-16/pt-18 are the documented floor and these sit well above it — kept in
// sync with the other *FloatingBadge files.
//
// titleleft/titleright are <p>, not headings: the column labels here are
// supporting chrome. The one docx heading this box carries is `title`, and `as`
// defaults to "h2" to match the flat H1 + H2 brief.
//
// The card is `isolate` and both blurs are `-z-10`, so they paint above the card
// background but below the slot content. No `relative z-10` wrapper is needed
// and none may be re-added.
//
// RENGER8888: a crimson frame and glow on a near-black maroon card, the deep
// blood red carrying the second blur, and the badge gradient running steel
// silver → crimson → blood red, the wordmark's own bevel.
---

<section class="my-10 flex w-full justify-center px-4 font-sans">
  <div
    class="relative isolate w-full max-w-7xl rounded-2xl border-2 border-[#e8121f]/35 bg-gradient-to-b from-[#160406]/95 to-[#080203]/95 p-8 pt-32 shadow-[0_10px_30px_rgba(232,18,31,0.2)] md:pt-28">
    <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-10 -bottom-16 -z-10 h-40 w-40 rounded-full bg-[#8f0c14]/35 blur-[60px]"></div>
    <div aria-hidden="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-16 -left-10 -z-10 h-40 w-40 rounded-full bg-[#e8121f]/28 blur-[60px]"></div>

    {
      title && (
        <div class="absolute -top-6 left-1/2 w-[92%] max-w-2xl -translate-x-1/2 rounded-lg border-2 border-[#e8121f]/45 bg-[#28080b] px-4 py-2.5 text-center shadow-[0_10px_30px_rgba(232,18,31,0.2)] sm:px-8">
          <HeadingTag class="bg-gradient-to-r from-[#e6ecf2] via-[#e8121f] to-[#8f0c14] bg-clip-text text-lg leading-normal font-black tracking-tight text-transparent uppercase sm:text-xl md:text-2xl">
            {title}
          </HeadingTag>
        </div>
      )
    }

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 md:grid-cols-[3fr_7fr] md:items-center">
      <article class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-[#f0dcdc]">
        {titleleft && <p class="text-2xl leading-normal font-bold text-[#ff2b38]">{titleleft}</p>}
        <slot name="left" />
      </article>

      <article class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-left text-base leading-relaxed text-[#f0dcdc] md:border-l md:border-[#e8121f]/30 md:pl-10">
        {titleright && <p class="text-2xl leading-normal font-bold text-[#ff2b38]">{titleright}</p>}
        <slot name="right" />
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
